{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d172-aa29-7082-8eff-67d931aefab6"},"sequence":197,"recorded_at":1780531400000389,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"cc58f923-5939-4fc8-a20e-d72a2117b375","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"cc58f923-5939-4fc8-a20e-d72a2117b375","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"cc58f923-5939-4fc8-a20e-d72a2117b375"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d173-48d0-7683-9a58-5b4bd8bf744c"},"task_id":"01a0d173-48d0-7683-9a58-5b4bd8bf744c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d173-48d0-7683-9a58-5b4bd8bf744c","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-8-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-1jmmqn) { full }' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:6000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Get full task record\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"ac\\\": \\\"Production behavior demonstrates: Plan pair-neutral target projection, checkpoint message authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata, and vendor importer strategies. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\\\",\\n \\\"assignee\\\": \\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\n \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-2ya5le\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"blocks\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260830-1esv6u\\\",\\n  \\\"TASK-260924-3n78rv\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Plan pair-neutral target projection, checkpoint message authority, inactive tools/instructions, token metadata, and vendor importer strategies\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Closed member sets and identities: Projection Plan 1.0.0 and Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 have exactly their members (reflection-derived member census, every member missing/extra/duplicated/wrong JSON type refused with a literal code) and their ids equal the JCS digest with only the id member omitted, recomputed independently in the test\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Structural rules by whole-domain enumeration against an independent oracle: ProjectionTargetOperation dependencies are strictly lower sequences and form a DAG (every small graph up to 5 operations enumerated), ExpectedTargetResource and ProjectedObjectEntry blob/directory nullability branch-exact over the full kind x field-presence grid, every sorted-unique array refused unsorted or duplicated, every length/cardinality bound at edge and edge+1, the closed plan constants (TransactionPlan, ReadBackPlan, ResumeProjectionPlan, RollbackPlan) refused on any other value\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate x entry census with an explicit axis inventory (for unbounded axes a generated range plus a structural argument), isolated kill attribution, importer outcome grid keyed (package, entry, input) with moved classes named, reuse of internal/canonicaljson and the landed internal/clonefidelity types; task_delta scope, no registry edit; planning semantics are out of scope (TASK-260924-3n78rv)\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"children\\\": [],\\n \\\"created\\\": \\\"2026-08-29T22:02:08Z\\\",\\n \\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\": [],\\n \\\"derivedBlocks\\\": [],\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"Projection Plan 1.0.0 and Clone Projected Object Manifest 1.0.0 as closed schemas (pinned SPEC v0.7.0 \\\\u00a713.14.2 from 10548, component schemas ~10640-10760): exact member sets, JCS identities under the omission rule, ProjectionTargetOperation DAG (dependencies are lower sequences), ExpectedTargetResource and ProjectedObjectEntry branch-exact nullability, sorting/uniqueness, Transaction/ReadBack/Resume/Rollback plan constants, ContractRequirement. Split 2026-09-24 by the orchestrator (one attack surface per leaf): planning semantics moved to a sibling leaf. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\\\",\\n \\\"estimate\\\": {\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"estimated\\\",\\n  \\\"scale\\\": {\\n   \\\"kin\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6001,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1501,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
